WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.769 --> 00:00:02.712
(upbeat piano music)

00:00:03.394 --> 00:00:05.344
- We don't have to clean.

00:00:05.344 --> 00:00:07.550
- What do you wanna do
with all our extra time?

00:00:08.423 --> 00:00:11.163
- We could make some
cold-pressed organic juices.

00:00:11.163 --> 00:00:13.485
- We could switch over
to paperless billing.

00:00:13.485 --> 00:00:15.156
- We could floss our teeth.

00:00:15.156 --> 00:00:17.014
- We could find out who my father is.

00:00:17.524 --> 00:00:18.973
Oh, my god.
(cat wails)

00:00:18.973 --> 00:00:20.125
- Oh, holy shit.

00:00:20.125 --> 00:00:22.232
- There's cat shit in the vacuum.

00:00:22.842 --> 00:00:25.808
(upbeat lounge music)

00:00:28.797 --> 00:00:30.365
- The thing looks sick, what does it do?

00:00:30.365 --> 00:00:32.036
- [Robot] I can check email, brew coffee,

00:00:32.036 --> 00:00:34.312
kill spiders, do therapy sessions,

00:00:34.312 --> 00:00:36.094
I can even dance.

00:00:36.158 --> 00:00:37.609
(group exclaims)

00:00:37.609 --> 00:00:39.670
(intense rap beat)

00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:41.457
- [Group] Go Gino, go Gino, go Gino

00:00:41.457 --> 00:00:42.434
- Great point, Gino.

00:00:42.434 --> 00:00:43.943
I feel like you are the only one here

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:45.794
who really understands me.

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:47.611
- You know, your robot
can't make out with you.

00:00:47.861 --> 00:00:49.607
- [Robot] I don't want him for his body.

00:00:49.607 --> 00:00:51.855
I like him for his mind.

00:00:52.154 --> 00:00:54.014
(upbeat lounge music)

00:00:55.267 --> 00:00:58.782
(phone ringing)

00:00:59.676 --> 00:01:00.308
- No, no, no, no, no.

00:01:00.308 --> 00:01:02.468
I just got a notification
that the milk's expired.

00:01:02.468 --> 00:01:04.070
- Oh my God, that could
have been really bad.

00:01:04.070 --> 00:01:05.602
- Shhh, come here.

00:01:05.602 --> 00:01:06.601
You're safe now.

00:01:06.601 --> 00:01:07.553
- Checking stats?

00:01:07.553 --> 00:01:08.667
How's Denver doing?

00:01:08.667 --> 00:01:11.152
- Oh, no I'm checking out the milk stats.

00:01:11.152 --> 00:01:12.150
The smart jug tells me all kinds

00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:13.775
of vital stuff about the milk.

00:01:13.775 --> 00:01:15.702
Expiration date, temperature,

00:01:15.702 --> 00:01:18.373
what farm the milk came
from, what percentage,

00:01:18.373 --> 00:01:20.300
cause you've got your
skim milk, you got 2%.

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:23.243
Yeah, just basically milk stuff.

00:01:25.638 --> 00:01:28.117
(upbeat lounge music)

00:01:28.117 --> 00:01:29.001
(phone ringing)

00:01:29.001 --> 00:01:30.069
- Oh, babe, don't answer it.

00:01:30.069 --> 00:01:31.184
It's gonna let all the heat out.

00:01:31.184 --> 00:01:33.227
- Babe, chillax, no inconvenience,

00:01:33.227 --> 00:01:35.382
I've got my bluetooth glove.

00:01:36.222 --> 00:01:36.754
Hello?

00:01:36.754 --> 00:01:38.163
(phone buzzing)

00:01:38.163 --> 00:01:40.593
Hello? Hello?

00:01:44.024 --> 00:01:46.316
(upbeat lounge music)

00:01:46.857 --> 00:01:48.180
- Aren't these USB slippers better

00:01:48.180 --> 00:01:49.572
than warming your icy toes

00:01:49.572 --> 00:01:51.733
on my extremely athletic calves?

00:01:53.854 --> 00:01:55.456
Alright, what are we watching?

00:01:55.456 --> 00:01:57.818
- Oh, let me run to the bathroom first.

00:01:58.568 --> 00:01:59.593
- No, wait, oh!

00:01:59.593 --> 00:02:02.035
(soothing lounge music)

00:02:03.795 --> 00:02:05.259
- Oh, the blinds. I'll get em.

00:02:05.259 --> 00:02:06.280
- No, no, no, no no,

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:08.714
Those feet are too adorbs
to walk another step.

00:02:08.714 --> 00:02:09.619
Here.

00:02:10.828 --> 00:02:12.728
(mechanical whirr)

00:02:12.757 --> 00:02:16.361
(constant mechanical whirr)

00:02:16.361 --> 00:02:17.490
- [Woman] Nooo.

00:02:21.025 --> 00:02:23.411
(upbeat lounge music)

00:02:24.624 --> 00:02:28.171
- Oh, Cindy Crawford,
you are the flyest cat.

00:02:28.640 --> 00:02:31.218
And it's all thanks to your
smart feeder, isn't it?

00:02:31.218 --> 00:02:33.215
You get the right portions every time.

00:02:33.965 --> 00:02:36.354
Yeah, that's where your food comes from.

00:02:44.444 --> 00:02:46.304
- [Woman] So much for portion control.

00:02:46.565 --> 00:02:48.580
- [Man] Cindy Crawford, you (beep).

